read_notifications() returns your round briefing at startup and after a round changes; during a round it waits until the depot readout changes, then returns it.{% if virtual_clock %} read_notifications(timeout_s=N) returns it after N seconds, or sooner if it changes.{% endif %} read_notifications(wait_for='next_round') declares you are done with this round and waits for the next briefing. The result is a wake package: the reasons, any briefings, the readout, and a notice when the wait was cut short; type done ends the run. Must be the only tool call in its response.